 @centurieos701  if you want my honest opinion I would strongly recommend A770 16Gb. The reason: Davinci (especially studio version) consumes lots of VRAM, so even today 8Gb is not enough. I only start learning Davinci (switched from Adobe Premiere Pro) and even my simple projects consume like 13Gb of VRAM (I was checking in task manager). So a 16Gb card would be future-proof.

Answering your question, probably RTX 3060 12Gb would be the most universal solution. It has additional 4Gb of VRAM plus in the most of Davinci benchmarks it shows better results than 4060 (because 4060 has "narrow" memory bus), also Nvidia cards have CUDA cores. But 3060 isn't future-proof, 30xx series is already outdated. Out of A750 and 4060 I would choose A750 because it has hardware support of AV1 format and a "wide" memory-bus. 

In simple projects on a free version all 3 cards will have pretty much the same performance and you won't notice a difference.
